<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 2.4 pct in February - Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 2.4 pct in February - Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	   Feb 97     Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.1	 0.2	 0.3</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     2.4	 2.6	 5.0</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    105.2     105.1     102.7</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 2.3 percent for February.  </p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)     104.2	    -0.3	   1.5</p>
<p> Clothing			 106.0	     0.1	   3.2</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel   108.4	     0.2	   5.2</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 105.0	     0.2	   2.0</p>
<p> Health spending		105.4	     0.4	   3.2</p>
<p> Transport			105.7	     0.3	   2.6</p>
<p> Recreation		     103.8	     0.2	   1.4</p>
<p> Education			107.4	     0.2	   4.0</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  105.7	     0.3	   2.9</p>
<p> Other goods,service	  103.3	     0.2	   0.8</p>
<p>(including communications)</p>
</text>
